            <div xml:id="d107-a2">

                <pb facs="0229" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg135"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 552.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Law declaring Madagascar and depending islands a
                        French colony.</hi></head>
                <p>The Senate and the Chamber of Deputies have adopted, and the President of the
                    Republic promulgates, the following law:</p>
                <p>Sole article: The island of Madagascar, with its depending islands, is declared
                    to be a French colony.</p>
                <p>The present law, debated and adopted by the Senate and the Chamber of Deputies,
                    shall be executed as a state law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Made at <placeName>Brest</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-08-06">August 6,
                        1896</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Félix Faure</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >President of the Republic.</hi></signed><lb/>By the minister of
                            colonies:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">André
                        Lebon.</hi></signed><lb/>The minister of foreign affairs:<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">G. Hanotaux.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
